{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"direction"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLUpDown","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLUpDownO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLUpDown"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"isUnbroken"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"position"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLPosition"},{"kind":"text","text":" = MXLPosition(), "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"placement"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAboveBelow","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil)"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"id","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The optional-unique-id attribute group allows an element to optionally specify an ID that is unique to the entire document. This attribute group is not used for a required id attribute, or for an id attribute that specifies an id reference.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"number","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Distinguishes between two simultaneous chords arpeggiated separately (different numbers) or together (same number).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"direction","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The direction of the arrow on the arpeggio sign, if present.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"isUnbroken","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A Boolean value indicating whether the arpeggio continues onto another staff within the part.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"position","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"placement","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a notation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"color","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"code":"MXLArpeggiate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate\/init(id:number:direction:isUnbroken:position:placement:color:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Initializer","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"direction"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLUpDownO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLUpDown"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"isUnbroken"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"position"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLPosition"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"placement"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?)"}],"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV2id6number9direction10isUnbroken8position9placement5colorACSSSg_AA14MXLNumberLevelVSgAA9MXLUpDownOSgSbSgAA11MXLPositionVAA13MXLAboveBelowOSgAA8MXLColorVSgtcfc","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"init","title":"init(id:number:direction:isUnbroken:position:placement:color:)"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate\/init(id:number:direction:isunbroken:position:placement:color:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAboveBelow":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The above-below type is used to indicate whether one element appears above or below another element.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"}],"title":"MXLAboveBelow","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlabovebelow","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAboveBelow"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Slurs, tuplets, and many other features can be concurrent and overlap within a single musical part. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number-level entity distinguishes up to 16 concurrent objects of the same type when the objects overlap in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"MusicXML document order. Values greater than 6 are usually only needed for music with a large number of divisi"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"staves in a single part, or if there are more than 6 cross-staff arpeggios in a single measure. When a number-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"level value is implied, the value is 1 by default."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLNumberLevel","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"abstract":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLPosition","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLUpDown":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlupdown","title":"MXLUpDown","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLUpDown"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLUpDown"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The up-down type is used for the direction of arrows and other pointed symbols like vertical accents,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indicating which way the tip is pointing.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLUpDown"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate/init(id:number:direction:isUnbroken:position:placement:color:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate\/init(id:number:direction:isunbroken:position:placement:color:)","title":"init(id:number:direction:isUnbroken:position:placement:color:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MXLArpeggiate"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"number","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"direction","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLUpDown","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLUpDownO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isUnbroken","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"position","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPosition","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"placement","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAboveBelow","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate\/init(id:number:direction:isUnbroken:position:placement:color:)"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLArpeggiate"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLArpeggiate"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The arpeggiate type indicates that this note is part of an arpeggiated chord. The number attribute can be used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to distinguish between two simultaneous chords arpeggiated separately (different numbers) or together (same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number). The direction attribute is used if there is an arrow on the arpeggio sign. By default, arpeggios go"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the lowest to highest note. The length of the sign can be determined from the position attributes for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arpeggiate elements used with the top and bottom notes of the arpeggiated chord. If the unbroken attribute is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set to yes, it indicates that the arpeggio continues onto another staff within the part. This serves as a hint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to applications and is not required for cross-staff arpeggios."}],"title":"MXLArpeggiate"}}}